Outputs
The module provides:

a GSEA result table;
a top-pathway dotplot;
a single-pathway enrichment curve using GseaVis;
CSV export of all GSEA results;
PDF export of the dotplot and enrichment curve.







WarningGSEA is not the same as over-representation analysis



GO/KEGG enrichment in the preceding chapter starts from a selected ID set. GSEA instead tests coordinated movement across a ranked list, which can detect pathway-level signals even when individual proteins do not cross a hard significance threshold.

Outputs
The module reports the number of proteins, taxa and functions and provides:

merged abundance/taxonomy/function table;
taxonomy composition plot;
function composition plot;
taxon-function Sankey diagram;
taxon-function heatmap;
downloadable merged table.

Where Load data comes from
The current loader uses this priority:

the active in-memory ProtVis_dataset;
Step2_remove_unreliable_peptide.rda;
Sage-specific compatibility snapshots such as Step2_sage_database_search.rda;
older project-stage fallbacks when required for recovery.

Step2_remove_unreliable_peptide.rda is now the canonical data-source-independent Step2 checkpoint, even though its historical filename originated in the MaxQuant workflow. A successful Raw/Sage search publishes its completed ProtVis_dataset to this same handoff.
If the current object is still Sage_staging, the expression table is intentionally unavailable. Complete Search before running Correct Noise.
